# Language & Localization

Music On Chain is a global product. The app already supports i18n.

## Rules

- **Default locale: Spanish (`es`)** — never default to English
- **Secondary locale: English (`en`)** — must keep working
- **Never hardcode** user-facing / visible text in components
- **All** UI strings live in `lib/i18n.ts` under both `es` and `en`
- Every new feature/component must ship **complete** `es` + `en` keys

## Usage

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1>Protocol</h1>

// ✅ GOOD
const t = getTranslations(locale);
<h1>{t.protocol.title}</h1>
```

Client components: `const locale = useLocale(); const t = getTranslations(locale);`  
Server components: `const locale = await getLocaleFromCookie(); const t = getTranslations(locale);`

## Tone

UI copy is investor-facing and premium (see `.cursor/rules/ux-copy.mdc`). Prefer concise product phrases over literal translations.

## Proper nouns & terminology

Follow `.cursor/rules/spanish-terminology.mdc` for Spanish UI vocabulary (Activo Musical, Regalía, Liquidación, Núcleo del Protocolo, etc.).

Brand names and API identifiers (e.g. `connectWallet`, Music On Chain, SDK, Wallet, Marketplace) stay as specified — never translate SDK method names.
